      "controls": {},
      "options": {},
      "values": {
        "text": {
          "Text": "A list into a maths node runs the maths once per item and gives a list back. Grid Points lays out 16 \u00d7 9 dots; Pythagorean takes each dot's X and Y and gives its distance from the middle, and the Sine of that distance, its Phase walked back by the Master Gear, is a wave rolling outward. Add 0.55 and every dot has a size, small in the troughs and big on the crests. Try the Sine's Frequency, or Grid Points' Columns and Rows."
        }
      },
      "width": 380.0
    },
